# === Raw / restricted-use patient identifiers ===
# RSNA 2019 is a restricted-use (Kaggle competition rules) dataset. Publishing
# raw PatientID values is a likely data-use-agreement violation. The public,
# hashed replacement (truncated SHA-256, matching Manuscript_G1_SCI_Full
# Section 4.4 / Supplementary Table S2) lives in data/*_hashed.json and IS
# committed — only the raw-ID file is excluded here.
data/bhsd_rsna_overlap_patient_ids.json
# BHSD's own dataset.json manifest: its imagesTr/imagesTs/labelsTr entries are
# filenames of the form ID_<rsna-format-patient-token>_ID_<study-token>.nii.gz
# -- i.e. it lists the same 192 raw RSNA-format patient identifiers as above,
# just sourced from BHSD's distribution instead of ours. Excluded for the same
# reason; obtain it directly from BHSD's own release if needed (see README).
data/bhsd/dataset.json

# === Model checkpoints / weights ===
# The manuscripts' Data and Code Availability statements state raw model
# checkpoints were not copied and remain server-only. Keep that true here.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.h5
*.safetensors

# === Raw dataset downloads ===
# Datasets are never included in this repo (each has its own license/DUA);
# these patterns guard against ever accidentally committing a real download
# staged locally under data/.
data/rsna/
data/cq500/
data/bhsd/images/
data/bhsd/masks/
*.dcm
*.nii
*.nii.gz

# === Superseded / noisy local artifacts (not part of the public evidence trail) ===
# Full untrimmed download log (progress-bar spam only, no unique content beyond
# the trimmed download_rsna.log that IS committed).
download_rsna.log.FULL_WITH_PROGRESS_BAR.bak_excluded_from_git
# Stale README snapshot from before real training ran; superseded by README.md,
# and its "no real numbers were produced" claim is no longer true.
README_hp100.md

